  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xE9;ponse sanitaire d&#x2019;urgence face aux cons&#xE9;quences de cyclone GAMANE dans les districts d&#x2019;ANTALAHA, SAMBAVA et VOHEMAR, r&#xE9;gion de SAVA, MADAGASCAR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">he main objective of this WHO project is to provide emergency health response to the consequences of Cyclone Gamane in the districts of Antalaha, Sambava, and Vohe&#x301;mar, Sava region, Madagascar. The project focuses on aiding vulnerable populations, providing free care packages, and maintaining access to health services. Efforts include acquiring and delivering essential medical supplies, rehabilitating health facilities, strengthening disease surveillance, conducting risk communication and community engagement activities, and enhancing monitoring and evaluation. WHO targets 22,239 people, including 5,251 women, 5,045 men, and 11,943 children.</narrative>
  </description>
